    "body": "fix on issue/1446-rest-2d · PR #1491 (draft, `Refs`, head 914c7f719) · pinned by `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs` (10 tests, e.g. `rest_area_is_the_four_corners_and_never_reads_small`, `rest_passes_cut_only_the_corners_and_cover_them`, `previous_tool_not_larger_is_refused_by_name`) · merges at the next cut\n\nFirst slice only, so this issue stays open when the PR merges: the motion-crate generator (`rest_plan`, `rest_pocket`; previous tool entered by hand; ring strategies). Quick gate green, clippy clean. Not run on a machine; no stock simulation; nothing wired to the operation, the UI, the project file or MCP yet.\n\nWhat is left is filed:\n- #1489 - the Pocket operation parameter (default off), undoable edit, project file, dialog group, MCP parameters, golden CL through the app, stock-simulation reading.\n- #1490 - Adaptive over a rest area, entry from already-cut space, previous tool from the carried stock, Zigzag.\n\nFound while testing (in `docs/decisions/1446-rest-2d.md`): Zigzag rows left residue in the corner, so Zigzag is refused by name with rest; fitted arcs crossed at the thin horns of a rest area, so the rest rings go through the existing crossing proof.\n",
